- **Breaking (v5.0.0):** every list API endpoint now returns bounded pages. Omitting `per_page` returns the first page (default 100 rows) instead of every row, and `per_page` values above 1,000 are clamped to 1,000. Pagination metadata (`meta`) is now returned by `GET /fleets`, `GET /users`, `GET /invites`, `GET /labels`, `GET /carves`, and the schedule endpoints. `GET /mdm/apple/devices`, `GET /commands/results`, `GET /hosts/:id/configuration_profiles`, `GET /hosts/:id/reports/:report_id`, and `GET /device/:token/policies` now accept `page`/`per_page` and return `meta`. Clients that relied on fetch-all must add a paging loop (the Fleet UI, fleetctl, and GitOps already do this transparently). `GET /hosts/report` (CSV export) intentionally remains a full export.
